kind.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-34ee9ff71eef4564a637474f51699aa9/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -o ShipmentTracker -int Auto -ai -au Individual --no-https`.

## Project Structure
- **ShipmentTracker/** (server project) - hosts app, has EF Core + Identity
- **ShipmentTracker.Client/** (client/WebAssembly project) - all interactive components go here
- Global Interactive Auto mode - no need to add @rendermode to pages
- Identity/auth already configured with SQLite

## CRITICAL Auto Mode Rules
- All interactive components MUST be in the `.Client` project
- `.Client` components cannot access DbContext or server-only services
- Data access must go through HTTP APIs (service interface in .Client, HttpClient impl in .Client, direct DB impl in server)
- Both Program.cs files must register matching services

## What to Implement

### 1. Shared Model - Create in .Client project (referenced by both)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed,
    Cancelled
}
```

### 2. Service Interface in .Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment?> GetByIdAsync(int id);
    Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
}
```

### 3. Client-side HttpClient Implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentServiceClient.cs` - uses HttpClient to call server APIs:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentServiceClient(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/{id}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
        => await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side Direct Implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServiceServer.cs` - uses EF Core directly:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServiceServer(ApplicationDbContext db) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.CreatedDate).ToListAsync();

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
        => await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetByIdAsync(int id)
        => await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);

    public async Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
            await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        shipment.TrackingNumber = $"ST-{DateTime.UtcNow:yyyyMMdd}-{Random.Shared.Next(10000, 99999)}";
        shipment.CreatedDate = DateTime.UtcNow;
        db.Shipments.Add(shipment);
        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }
}
```

### 5. Update ApplicationDbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add Shipments DbSet:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
